So anyway, here you are standing around acting like a petulant child instead of accepting that the universe doesn’t give a flying fuck about you.
If I were your mother and had raised someone so self-involved, it wouldn’t surprise me that you have trouble with empathy. It also makes sense why you didn’t have the capacity for love;

I will start with some stats from my local domestic abuse agency, based on cases reported to their helpline in 2020, as provided by them via Freedom Of Information request, which are presented below:
-Domestic violence occurs every 20.2 seconds. In one hour, it happens once to every 3.1 women and men;
-A person is abused by an intimate or romantic partner in a relationship (current, ex, or former) once every 8 minutes and 43 seconds on average, and an abuser has assaulted, injured, threatened, forced a sexual or non-sexual act upon someone in an intimate or sexual partnership on more than 6 occasions each and every year;
–A survivor will be assaulted with physical, verbal, or psychological abuse at some point over the next 12 months.

